cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CiteGuard MCP: Zero-Dependency Model Context Protocol Server and CLI for Scientific Citation Verification, Chimera Hallucination Detection, and Retraction Screening"
message: "If you use CiteGuard MCP in your research, manuscripts, or AI workflows, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Luca
    family-names: Celebrano
    email: luca.celebrano1@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Naples, Italy"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0931-3555"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lukecele/citeguard-mcp"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/citeguard-mcp/"
abstract: >-
  Zero-dependency Python Model Context Protocol (MCP) server and command-line
  interface (CLI) that verifies scientific citations (DOIs, PubMed PMIDs, and
  arXiv IDs) in real time across Crossref, DataCite (CERN Zenodo), PubMed (NCBI
  E-utilities), OpenAlex, and arXiv. Detects fabricated identifiers, LLM
  chimera metadata mismatches (valid DOIs paired with fabricated titles,
  authors, or years), and formally retracted papers, and generates canonical
  BibTeX bibliographies.
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp-server
  - citation-verification
  - hallucination-detection
  - retraction-screening
  - bibtex
  - crossref
  - pubmed
  - openalex
  - arxiv
  - scientific-writing
license: MIT
